{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"kind":"symbol","relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/JSONObjectEncodable","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/JSONValueDecodable","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/JSONValueEncodable","doc:\/\/Readium\/SQ","doc:\/\/Readium\/SH","doc:\/\/Readium\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Readium\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/DOMRange"},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/DOMRange\/Point"],"generated":true,"title":"Structures"},{"anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/DOMRange\/init(json:warnings:)","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/DOMRange\/init(start:end:)"],"generated":true,"title":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/DOMRange\/jsonObject"],"title":"Instance Properties","generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/DOMRange\/Equatable-Implementations","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/DOMRange\/JSONObjectEncodable-Implementations","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/DOMRange\/JSONValueDecodable-Implementations","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/DOMRange\/JSONValueEncodable-Implementations"],"title":"Default Implementations","generated":true,"anchor":"Default-Implementations"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DOMRange"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["iOS","iPadOS","Mac Catalyst"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"In a DOM Range object, the startContainer + startOffset tuple represents the ","type":"text"},{"code":"start","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" boundary","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"point. Similarly, the the endContainer + endOffset tuple represents the ","type":"text"},{"code":"end","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" boundary point.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"In both cases, the start\/endContainer property is a pointer to either a DOM text node, or a DOM","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"element (this typically depends on the mechanism from which the DOM Range instance originates,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for example when obtaining the currently-selected document fragment using the ","type":"text"},{"code":"window.selection","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"API). In the case of a DOM text node, the start\/endOffset corresponds to a position within the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"character data. In the case of a DOM element node, the start\/endOffset corresponds to a position","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that designates a child text node.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Note that ","type":"text"},{"code":"end","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" field is optional. When only the start field is specified, the domRange object","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"represents a “collapsed” range that has identical ","type":"text"},{"code":"start","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"end","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" boundary points.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"https:\/\/github.com\/readium\/architecture\/blob\/master\/models\/locators\/extensions\/html.md#the-domrange-object","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"This construct enables a serializable representation of a DOM Ran